1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:18,000
MethaneResponse helps analysts examine methane claims against traceable evidence.
It supports UNEP MARS; it does not detect methane or replace it.

2
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:36,000
This prototype uses a versioned historical MARS snapshot.
The feed is not live.

3
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:57,000
The snapshot contains 4,218 source locations and 30,414 plume records,
with observations through 13 September 2026 UTC.

4
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:15,000
6,553 plume rows have no source ID and remain unlinked.
A mapped source is not automatically a fully audited case.

5
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:31,000
KAZ_S_159 is a historical oil and gas source in Kazakhstan.
Its recorded coordinates are 43.41337° N, 52.91829° E.

6
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:54,000
MARS links three dated plume observations to this source.
The latest shown is 496 ± 226 kg/h on 11 July 2026 (EnMAP-DLR).

7
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:09,000
That is a satellite-estimated value for one observation,
not current flux or continuous monitoring.

8
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:27,000
The claim under review is that the detected release was mitigated.
The deterministic rules baseline returns “insufficient evidence.”

9
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:39,000
The linked report text is not included in this assessment.
Missing later observations do not prove zero emissions or repair.

10
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:59,000
The recurrence panel concerns a later linked MARS archive record,
not a forecast of future leakage, emissions, or mitigation.

11
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:18,000
The verifier page separates audit bundles from blockchain receipts.
This screen lists one bundle and zero anchored receipts.

12
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:38,000
No Sepolia transaction is shown in this recording.
A cryptographic digest cannot establish that mitigation occurred.

13
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:58,000
No Sepolia transaction or blockchain receipt is shown in this run.
Blockchain anchoring is not configured for this recording.

14
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:18,800
No live AI provider or authenticated human review ran here.
User benefit and emissions impact still require independent evaluation.
